lisa-design:
- Extra split (beyond the spec's exec/eval split): the eval layer was 1311 changed lines, so the behaviour-neutral restructuring of Eval lands first in ra/w2-c7n-eval-scopes and the accounts logic in ra/w2-c7n-accounts-eval on top. Each PR stays under 1000 lines (non-negotiable rule).
- Eval's per-run state moved from locals into evalRun, and the baseline + check loop into evalScope(scope) with the scope's output root and regions; collectInventoryBaselines takes the scope; request construction is one helper (executionRequest). With one scope, every request, log, payload, evidence and error is unchanged.
- Proof of no behaviour change: TestEvalWithoutAccountsMatchesGolden records requests (output dirs relative to the execution root, regions, account fields), labels, subjects, full payload JSON, evidence UUIDs (seeded from labels like policy-manager), CreateEvidence calls, status and error. The golden (testdata/eval_without_accounts.golden, one JSON value per line) was recorded in the two test commits before this refactor and must not be regenerated to make a later change pass.
